        "text": "For tonight, I’d shortlist these, given your interest in nature, photography, and gripping real-life stories:\n\n- **My Octopus Teacher** (2020, 85 min) — A filmmaker follows a wild octopus in a South African kelp forest. Beautiful underwater photography and an intimate story—ideal for a quieter evening.\n- **The Rescue** (2021, 107 min) — About the rescue of a Thai youth football team trapped in a flooded cave. If you liked the tension of *Free Solo*, this is my strongest pick.\n- **Chasing Coral** (2017, 89 min) — Divers and photographers document coral bleaching, making an enormous environmental issue tangible. Visually striking, but sobering.\n- **Finding Vivian Maier** (2013, 83 min) — An investigation into a nanny whose extraordinary street photography was largely discovered after her death. A good fit for your photography and storytelling interests.\n- **Searching for Sugar Man** (2012, 86 min) — Two fans investigate what happened to an elusive musician. Go in knowing as little as possible.\n\n**My vote: *The Rescue* for suspense, or *My Octopus Teacher* to unwind.** Streaming availability varies by country."
